    "text": "To determine the number of shirt-and-tie outfits that can be made without wearing a shirt and a tie of the same color, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of possible outfits without any restrictions:**\n   - There are 8 colors, and for each color, there is one shirt and one tie.\n   - Therefore, the total number of possible outfits (where each shirt is paired with each tie) is:\n     \\[\n     8 \\text{ (shirts)} \\times 8 \\text{ (ties)} = 64 \\text{ outfits}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Identify the number of outfits that violate the restriction:**\n   - The restriction is that a shirt and a tie cannot be of the same color.\n   - For each color, there is exactly one shirt and one tie, so there is only one outfit where the shirt and tie are of the same color (the shirt and tie of that color).\n   - Since there are 8 colors, there are:\n     \\[\n     8 \\text{ outfits} \\text{ that violate the restriction}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of valid outfits:**\n   - Subtract the number of outfits that violate the restriction from the total number of possible outfits:\n     \\[\n     64 \\text{ (total outfits)} - 8 \\text{ (outfits violating the restriction)} = 56 \\text{ valid outfits}\n     \\]\n\nThus, the number of shirt-and-tie outfits that can be made without wearing a shirt and a tie of the same color is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{56}\n\\]",
